1
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,360
Hey!

2
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,520
Let me help pick them up.

3
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,560
It's okay.

4
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,760
What happened in there?

5
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,760
Din, let's just go.

6
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,760
I'll tell you later.

7
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:16,680
Then from now on, I'll take you to class every day

8
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:18,440
and wait to pick you up, too.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,240
Let him do whatever he wants. Don't worry about me.

10
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,680
I don't want to go back anymore.

11
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,080
There was one I really liked,

12
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:25,720
but it's not in London.

13
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,640
What do you think?

14
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,960
Study together, or somewhere else?

15
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:32,159
But if we're going together, the same city is easier.

16
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:34,920
And when you're free, go check out the seniors' work at uni.

17
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,400
Even if you get some letters right,

18
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,200
you'll never guess the last three.

19
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,280
Peel some for me too, son.

20
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:42,120
Here you go, sir. All peeled.

21
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,720
I'll probably be late on match day.

22
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:44,920
Going to an open house first.

23
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:47,440
I swim so my lungs get stronger.

24
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:49,440
So I can run all day, morning to night.

25
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:51,480
The reason I never gave you a chance

26
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,000
is you're all talk,

27
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,200
you never really show it.

28
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,680
But this time, you're proving it to everyone around you.

29
00:00:56,680 --> 00:00:57,520
Not just me.

30
00:00:57,520 --> 00:00:58,640
At the match this Sunday,

31
00:00:58,640 --> 00:00:59,800
I'll score five goals alone.

32
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:00,920
But if you can't do it...

33
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,240
please keep your promise.

34
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,200
I can't let you do that.

35
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,760
Or you'll be their target all game.

36
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:05,920
But I have to win today.

37
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,600
And I'll score five goals on my own.

38
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:10,200
Then why are you here?

39
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,039
Does Physics know?

40
00:01:12,039 --> 00:01:13,400
Then why didn't you just tell me?

41
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,120
Why hide it?

42
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,680
I was so damn happy when you said you wanted to go together.

43
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:20,160
If you'd rather stay here, just tell me.

44
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:21,440
You don't have to come with me.

45
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:22,720
It's your life, Fuen.

46
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:00,200
Fuen?

47
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:04,000
What's wrong?

48
00:02:10,479 --> 00:02:12,440
I hurt Physics.

49
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:15,880
I didn't fucking think it through.

50
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:21,960
Fuen, can you tell us

51
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,000
what happened?

52
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:30,440
I went to the open house

53
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,400
and I just assumed

54
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,120
it'd be fine.

55
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,680
I was only going to look.

56
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,440
But Physics thinks

57
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,800
I'm thinking of not going with him.

58
00:02:50,480 --> 00:02:52,480
I've already decided, Chemi.

59
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,600
I'm not having second thoughts.

60
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,000
I'm just scared.

61
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,440
Scared of being a burden to him.

62
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,640
Scared I won't get in.

63
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,680
Aof...

64
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,079
Just now, he talked like

65
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,400
he'd be fine without me.

66
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,360
Or am I the only one

67
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:27,000
who can't live without him?

68
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,960
I'm not great with feelings and stuff like this.

69
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:39,440
Just trust me this once.

70
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:43,120
Go find Physics right now.

71
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:51,040
Fuen, Physics loves you way more than you think.

72
00:03:52,040 --> 00:03:53,480
Trust me on this.

73
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,240
He's right, Fuen.

74
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,560
My brother loves you so much.

75
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,640
He really does.

76
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:15,800
Did I get this one right?

77
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:30,560
"Snacks are out front after class, champ. Study hard."

78
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,480
Get some sleep.

79
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,920
You can study again tomorrow.

80
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,880
But I haven't memorized it all yet.

81
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:52,000
It's fine. I'll help you.

82
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,920
Don't worry.

83
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,480
Thanks a lot.

84
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:11,520
And...

85
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,880
Congrats.

86
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,240
But this time, take good care of Chemi.

87
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,560
Don't break his heart again.

88
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,400
Don't worry about me this time.

89
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:30,080
Worry about yourself.

90
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,680
Why'd you have to say that?

91
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,800
You okay?

92
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,159
Chill.

93
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,280
I'm fine. Chill.

94
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:02,560
Let's go to school together tomorrow.

95
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:07,360
Isn't your leg hurt, Aof?

96
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:11,680
And coming this way from your place is a detour.

97
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,080
We can just meet at school.

98
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:14,120
It's fine.

99
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:16,000
I'm an athlete.

100
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,400
Piece of cake.

101
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:22,240
Don't forget, we've never gone to school together.

102
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:26,320
And once I graduate from this school,

103
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:29,560
we'll never get the chance to go together again.

104
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,360
Hmm.

105
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,480
Okay.

106
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:41,400
But don't make me late.

107
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:43,520
I'll be here bright and early tomorrow.

108
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,680
Aof.

109
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:56,000
I don't know what will happen to us from here.

110
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,840
But I'll forget everything that happened before

111
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:09,000
and get to know you all over again.

112
00:09:11,880 --> 00:09:15,200
This is the last time.

113
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,320
Do it right.

114
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,880
I don't want to get hurt again.

115
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,320
Thank you, Chemi,

116
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,520
for giving me another chance.

117
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:43,720
I promise from now on,

118
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:45,960
I won't give you a reason to let go of me again.

119
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:55,280
Before, I didn't know how to set priorities.

120
00:09:57,800 --> 00:10:00,320
I got my priorities all wrong.

121
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,400
But now I know

122
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,720
how much you mean to me.

123
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,080
From now on, I promise

124
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:15,320
you'll be in every thought I have.

125
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:18,720
I won't do anything that hurts you.

126
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,720
I won't do anything wrong.

127
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:40,080
I still want to be the best version

128
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:41,800
of myself for you.

129
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:19,640
Thank you.

130
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:32,520
I'm going.

131
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,520
You can go home now.

132
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,480
Go on in. I'll wait right here.

133
00:11:39,120 --> 00:11:40,240
Are you limping?

134
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,160
It doesn't hurt.

135
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:44,960
Okay.

136
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,960
I'm going now.

137
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,040
Bye-bye.

138
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:04,560
Ow, it hurts. Damn, what a day. It fucking hurts. Shit.

139
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:59,200
What are you doing out here alone?

140
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,520
You okay?

141
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,640
Oh!

142
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,720
Hi, Mom.

143
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:24,320
What brings you here so late?

144
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:27,040
Um, Mom, is Physics home yet?

145
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,840
Not yet. He's not home yet.

146
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,520
Didn't you two meet up?

147
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:36,000
He told me he was sleeping over at your place.

148
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,440
Is something going on?

149
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:43,040
Oh, no, Mom.

150
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:45,000
Physics is probably at my place.

151
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,120
Don't worry.

152
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,400
Okay. But if he comes home, I'll call you.

153
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:53,600
Okay. Thank you so much. Bye.

154
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,160
So you're hurt

155
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,600
because you think he'd rather study

156
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:08,280
somewhere else than go with you, right?

157
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:14,000
Then let me tell you, that's not true.

158
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,160
Fuen wants to go with you.

159
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,960
He told me so himself.

160
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,440
The only problem is

161
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,240
he hasn't told his parents yet.

162
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,160
He's afraid his mom won't be okay with it

163
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:27,080
and that he won't get into any university this year.

164
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:33,080
But my guess is he's worried about his portfolio.

165
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,120
And I'm the one

166
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:37,120
who told him

167
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:38,880
to go see some really good work.

168
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:44,800
I get it,

169
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,840
why you're hurt.

170
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:50,040
But try to understand Fuen, too.

171
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,360
He's an only child.

172
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,840
Before you came along,

173
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:57,560
he always did everything on his own.

174
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:04,120
So sometimes he might forget to tell you things,

175
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:06,440
or he figures

176
00:15:06,440 --> 00:15:08,080
it's no big deal,

177
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:09,400
so he doesn't mention it.

178
00:15:12,160 --> 00:15:13,600
But I think he knows now

179
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:16,120
that it's causing problems between you two.

180
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,960
Do you think Fuen will change his mind?

181
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:28,760
Ask Fuen.

182
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,560
How would I know?

183
00:16:02,560 --> 00:16:04,080
Talk it out, okay?

184
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,360
Do you know everywhere I looked for you?

185
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,960
You weren't fucking anywhere.

186
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:30,160
You told me

187
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:33,160
you hate it when I leave you.

188
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,280
I hate it too.

189
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:07,720
I don't fucking care anymore.

190
00:17:08,319 --> 00:17:10,480
Over there, I'm going to be your burden.

191
00:17:10,480 --> 00:17:12,359
You'll have to take care of everything for me.

192
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:13,800
It's your own fault.

193
00:17:14,599 --> 00:17:17,599
You spoiled me. I can't even do what I used to.

194
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:27,440
You said we'd go together.

195
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:29,960
You sold me a dream,

196
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:31,960
and then you ditched me.

197
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,480
That's so damn irresponsible.

198
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:39,360
I like taking care of you,

199
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,560
looking out for you,

200
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:45,880
seeing you eat well and sleep well.

201
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:50,080
I want to take you everywhere with me.

202
00:17:51,800 --> 00:17:53,720
But I'm scared

203
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,240
that my love will end up hurting you again.

204
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:00,560
Hurt me how?

205
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:03,400
It's like my dad always said.

206
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,400
If it weren't you,

207
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:06,000
no one could put up with me.

208
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:14,920
Physics, I promise

209
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:18,320
I'll talk to you more,

210
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:21,200
even about the little things.

211
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:25,560
Whatever you ask me,

212
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:27,360
I'll answer all of it.

213
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,280
I promise.

214
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:31,960
Mm.

215
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:39,240
And I promise, too,

216
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:42,840
I won't let my head

217
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,280
convince me you don't need me anymore.

218
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:12,680
I'm glad I have you by my side.

219
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:34,800
I'm sorry.

220
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,200
I'm so sorry.

221
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:09,840
"Anyone still up? Look at the sky."

222
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:29,680
"The stars are pretty tonight. It's late, go to bed."

223
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:04,760
Don't make me late.

224
00:21:04,760 --> 00:21:05,760
Don't be late.

225
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:19,320
Hi, Mom.

226
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:20,320
How are you, dear?

227
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:21,480
I'm good.

228
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:23,360
I'm off, Mom.

229
00:22:23,360 --> 00:22:24,640
Bye.

230
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:27,800
Goodbye.

231
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:30,080
Aof.

232
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:31,360
Yes, Mom?

233
00:22:33,080 --> 00:22:35,000
Take good care of him.

234
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,320
Yes, Mom.

235
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:19,320
That looks so good.

236
00:23:20,480 --> 00:23:22,520
Looks good, so eat up.

237
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,280
How is it? Tasty?

238
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,120
It's good.

239
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:33,920
I can feed myself. I'm almost done.

240
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:35,720
Your hands hold the book,

241
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:37,040
your eyes read it.

242
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:39,200
As for your mouth, I'll feed you.

243
00:23:49,880 --> 00:23:51,840
Can I court you, Time?

244
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:17,720
Star, I have to go take my exam.

245
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:19,600
I'll probably be back this evening.

246
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,520
When you get to class,

247
00:24:22,520 --> 00:24:24,920
can you post a story so I know?

248
00:24:26,880 --> 00:24:28,080
Sure.

249
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:31,800
And give it your all today, Din.

250
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:35,120
I hope everything goes the way you want.

251
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:37,200
Thanks.

252
00:24:38,520 --> 00:24:41,520
When your class is over, wait for me there.

253
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:43,040
I'll come get you.

254
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:47,640
Okay. See you later, Din.

255
00:25:07,520 --> 00:25:08,600
You said 999!

256
00:25:09,400 --> 00:25:11,040
Why is it tens of thousands, Physics?

257
00:25:12,600 --> 00:25:13,920
It said 999 in the photo.

258
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:18,000
The actual guitar has a 3 and a 9 tacked on the front.

259
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:19,560
How about that?

260
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:22,160
See the perks of being an only child now?

261
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:24,160
I see the perks of being the youngest.

262
00:25:24,800 --> 00:25:26,600
Can I help you?

263
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:29,240
You've got a good eye.

264
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:31,280
But actually, this one's reserved.

265
00:25:31,760 --> 00:25:33,320
But if you really want it...

266
00:25:33,320 --> 00:25:35,120
Someone reserved it?

267
00:25:35,680 --> 00:25:38,000
Is the person who reserved it a boy

268
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:39,360
about this tall,

269
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:41,160
kind of Chinese-looking,

270
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:43,160
with bangs,

271
00:25:44,320 --> 00:25:46,680
who comes here a lot to buy guitar picks?

272
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:47,760
That's him.

273
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:50,440
Oh, if that's the case,

274
00:25:51,080 --> 00:25:54,280
you can just sell it to me.

275
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:56,520
That's my little brother.

276
00:25:57,040 --> 00:25:59,680
Mm. You got it, kid.

277
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:08,640
How's that, big brother?

278
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:12,200
There goes your allowance this term.

279
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:15,760
I'm afraid it won't just be this term.

280
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:29,600
There's a new milk tea place. Want to try it?

281
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:31,120
Really? Where is it?

282
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:33,680
Don't know. We can look it up.

283
00:27:03,920 --> 00:27:05,640
You studying hard?

284
00:27:06,960 --> 00:27:08,840
I'm studying hard!

285
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:14,080
"Made it to tutoring."

286
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,200
Hello, everyone.

287
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:21,600
Open your handouts to page three.

288
00:27:30,560 --> 00:27:32,240
Um, you're Phoodin, right?

289
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:33,240
Yes.

290
00:27:33,240 --> 00:27:34,720
Okay, you're up next.

291
00:27:34,720 --> 00:27:36,240
How was this morning? Did it go well?

292
00:27:36,240 --> 00:27:37,600
I think I did okay.

293
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:40,280
Hmm. Nervous?

294
00:27:40,280 --> 00:27:41,520
Yes, I am.

295
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:43,040
Oh, there's no need to be nervous.

296
00:27:43,040 --> 00:27:45,200
I peeked at your portfolio. You're in for sure.

297
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:46,200
Thank you so much.

298
00:27:46,200 --> 00:27:47,760
Okay, wait here.

299
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:10,360
Aren't you going to tell him, Rei?

300
00:28:10,840 --> 00:28:13,120
Yeah, I think you should tell him.

301
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:16,640
You're going to study over there with no plans to come back.

302
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:22,200
Nah. I think I'd better not.

303
00:28:22,640 --> 00:28:23,440
Forget it.

304
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:26,640
You have to tell him, man.

305
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,520
No way. You've got to tell him.

306
00:28:28,520 --> 00:28:29,520
No.

307
00:28:33,240 --> 00:28:35,880
Can you take notes for me? I'm going to the toilet.

308
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,040
Sure, sure.

309
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:16,920
Star.

310
00:29:17,880 --> 00:29:19,200
What's wrong?

311
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:21,400
Don't you remember me?

312
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:25,160
You smiled at me that day.

313
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,560
Hey!

314
00:29:28,560 --> 00:29:29,680
Why are you running away?

315
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:32,520
We know each other, don't we?

316
00:29:33,280 --> 00:29:34,560
It's me! / Hey!

317
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:36,080
The one who gave you snacks.

318
00:29:36,080 --> 00:29:37,200
Can you let me go?

319
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:38,880
Stay still! / Hey!

320
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:41,000
And my snacks?

321
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,880
Why'd you give them to other people?

322
00:29:44,040 --> 00:29:45,520
You led me on.

323
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:46,800
And now

324
00:29:48,440 --> 00:29:50,080
I like you.

325
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:52,280
Please let me go.

326
00:30:00,120 --> 00:30:01,920
Hey, where's Star?

327
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:03,440
He went to the toilet a while ago.

328
00:30:03,440 --> 00:30:04,440
He's still not back.

329
00:30:04,440 --> 00:30:05,600
Thanks.

330
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:08,720
Hey!

331
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:09,560
Hey, what's wrong?

332
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:10,960
Why are you hiding?

333
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:13,160
I don't like this!

334
00:30:13,160 --> 00:30:14,880
You psycho!

335
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,200
Star!

336
00:30:21,520 --> 00:30:22,520
Hey!

337
00:30:32,160 --> 00:30:33,160
Talk nicely?

338
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,080
Talk nicely, huh?

339
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:38,560
Look!

340
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:42,920
Then why'd you cheat on me with him?

341
00:30:44,280 --> 00:30:48,760
But it doesn't matter anymore, because today you're mine.

342
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:50,360
No, no!

343
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:53,960
Help!

344
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,480
Hold still.

345
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:58,320
I said hold still!

346
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:04,000
Help! Help me!

347
00:31:05,120 --> 00:31:07,040
Help!

348
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:20,240
Help! / Star!

349
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:23,800
What the fuck, you bastard?

350
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:26,680
What are you doing, you animal?

351
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:28,560
Rei!

352
00:31:29,480 --> 00:31:30,360
Let go of me, dammit!

353
00:31:30,360 --> 00:31:31,600
Shit, you'll kill him!

354
00:31:31,720 --> 00:31:32,720
Rei!

355
00:31:32,720 --> 00:31:33,480
Let go!

356
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:34,480
Go check on Star.

357
00:31:34,480 --> 00:31:35,480
I'll handle this.

358
00:31:38,760 --> 00:31:39,760
Star.

359
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:46,960
It's okay now, Star.

360
00:31:48,040 --> 00:31:49,680
That psycho can't hurt you anymore.

361
00:32:01,360 --> 00:32:02,240
Din.

362
00:32:03,360 --> 00:32:05,360
Star got attacked by a psycho.

363
00:32:18,360 --> 00:32:19,720
Star, are you okay?

364
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:33,640
Does Din know yet?

365
00:32:47,040 --> 00:32:47,960
Star.

366
00:32:47,960 --> 00:32:49,200
Din...

367
00:33:14,320 --> 00:33:16,560
I'm sorry I'm late.

368
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:21,640
Thanks for helping Star, man.

369
00:33:22,840 --> 00:33:24,760
Star's like a brother to me, too.

370
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:31,960
Told your dad?

371
00:33:32,640 --> 00:33:34,360
Dad and Samai are on their way.

372
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:37,600
Good. I'll stay with you.

373
00:33:38,280 --> 00:33:39,400
You're okay now.

374
00:33:47,240 --> 00:33:48,760
Star! / Dad!

375
00:33:51,680 --> 00:33:54,280
Are you okay, Star? Are you hurt anywhere?

376
00:33:55,360 --> 00:33:56,280
I'll take care of it.

377
00:33:57,720 --> 00:34:00,480
Din, please look after Star.

378
00:34:00,840 --> 00:34:01,600
Yes, sir.

379
00:34:02,360 --> 00:34:04,840
I'm sorry I didn't look after him better.

380
00:34:05,920 --> 00:34:07,760
Don't blame yourself.

381
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:09,280
It's not your fault.

382
00:34:11,719 --> 00:34:12,800
I'll be right back.

383
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:15,560
How's it going?

384
00:34:29,120 --> 00:34:31,120
I'll head off, then.

385
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,320
Let's go, guys.

386
00:34:32,320 --> 00:34:33,320
Rei.

387
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:37,880
Thank you, Rei.

388
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:40,639
No problem. Like I said, you can always come to me.

389
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:42,560
But you should tell him first.

390
00:34:43,600 --> 00:34:44,320
I'm off.

391
00:34:50,280 --> 00:34:51,199
Um, Din,

392
00:34:51,199 --> 00:34:53,239
please take care of Star.

393
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:03,720
Din.

394
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:09,120
Stay and talk with me for a bit.

395
00:35:22,320 --> 00:35:23,760
Does it hurt, Star?

396
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,560
Din,

397
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:11,720
you know what?

398
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:15,600
When I was being attacked,

399
00:36:17,640 --> 00:36:19,600
besides my dad, the one I thought of

400
00:36:22,840 --> 00:36:23,960
was you.

401
00:36:28,840 --> 00:36:31,400
All I could think was that I can't die yet.

402
00:36:33,880 --> 00:36:35,520
I still want to see my dad.

403
00:36:36,680 --> 00:36:38,840
I still want to wake up and see you.

404
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,360
You're so small.

405
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:57,200
How are you this strong?

406
00:37:03,480 --> 00:37:05,080
I guess it's the love I get from my dad

407
00:37:08,200 --> 00:37:09,320
and from you.

408
00:37:11,280 --> 00:37:13,320
It tells me that if one day

409
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:15,520
I start thinking about this again,

410
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:18,560
I won't be alone.

411
00:37:27,720 --> 00:37:29,800
I promise I'll take good care of you.

412
00:37:37,600 --> 00:37:39,600
So...

413
00:37:39,600 --> 00:37:42,280
How did your exam go today?

414
00:38:05,160 --> 00:38:06,280
Hello?

415
00:38:06,640 --> 00:38:07,640
Din.

416
00:38:07,880 --> 00:38:10,120
Star got attacked by a psycho.

417
00:38:10,120 --> 00:38:11,680
But he's safe now.

418
00:38:11,680 --> 00:38:12,960
I called the police.

419
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:14,800
Excuse me, you're up next.

420
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:16,120
You okay?

421
00:38:16,120 --> 00:38:16,760
Okay.

422
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:23,080
Is something wrong?

423
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:24,640
Sorry?

424
00:38:26,520 --> 00:38:27,440
Nervous?

425
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:30,400
You really want to study here?

426
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:34,640
Um, I like the program here.

427
00:38:34,640 --> 00:38:37,520
I think I'd be happy studying here.

428
00:38:40,200 --> 00:38:44,200
Then tell me why you don't look happy at all.

429
00:38:57,320 --> 00:38:59,360
It's because of me, isn't it, Din?

430
00:38:59,760 --> 00:39:01,200
I just couldn't focus.

431
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:09,000
Did you answer the professor?

432
00:39:13,680 --> 00:39:16,920
And what if they don't pass you? What will you do?

433
00:39:16,920 --> 00:39:19,800
It's fine, Star. I might still pass.

434
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:25,680
This is my fault, isn't it, Din?

435
00:39:26,200 --> 00:39:28,080
If I hadn't gotten in your head,

436
00:39:28,080 --> 00:39:29,920
you'd have done fine.

437
00:39:30,880 --> 00:39:31,680
Star.

438
00:39:33,640 --> 00:39:34,640
Say I don't pass,

439
00:39:35,320 --> 00:39:36,360
I've got the quota round.

440
00:39:37,080 --> 00:39:39,240
So don't overthink it, okay?

441
00:39:39,240 --> 00:39:40,240
Trust me.

442
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:42,240
I'll wait until results day.

443
00:39:43,760 --> 00:39:46,400
If you really don't get in,

444
00:39:47,640 --> 00:39:49,520
I'll be the one to tell your family.

445
00:40:42,640 --> 00:40:44,280
Why didn't you tell me?

446
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:50,120
Who would've thought

447
00:40:51,120 --> 00:40:53,040
you'd just leave them sitting there?

448
00:40:54,000 --> 00:40:57,400
Well, you said to use them when the power's out.

449
00:40:58,520 --> 00:41:00,480
My power never goes out.

450
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:10,760
"I like you. Give me a chance."

451
00:41:12,400 --> 00:41:14,720
"Can you not like anyone else? I get jealous."

452
00:41:23,040 --> 00:41:26,520
"Hope every day is a good day, and that you finally see I like you."

453
00:41:41,240 --> 00:41:42,800
Fuen.

454
00:41:46,280 --> 00:41:48,040
I gave you one every birthday.

455
00:41:52,520 --> 00:41:54,200
You even helped me hit on someone else.

456
00:41:56,480 --> 00:41:57,720
Well,

457
00:42:00,440 --> 00:42:01,960
you sweet-talked me.

458
00:42:04,280 --> 00:42:05,160
Hey.

459
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:12,880
Ever been sweet-talked by someone you like?

460
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:19,040
Right now.

461
00:42:23,720 --> 00:42:25,840
I'm not sweet-talking.

462
00:43:33,720 --> 00:43:35,840
Read the last message carefully.

463
00:43:43,240 --> 00:43:45,600
"I love you."

464
00:43:58,880 --> 00:44:00,400
If we get together,

465
00:44:00,760 --> 00:44:02,120
will we break up?

466
00:44:11,680 --> 00:44:14,120
I never saw you as just a friend to begin with.

467
00:44:20,160 --> 00:44:21,200
I won't break up.

468
00:44:45,120 --> 00:44:46,560
I love you, too.

469
00:45:39,760 --> 00:45:41,160
I've never kissed anyone before.

470
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:46,760
As if I have.

471
00:46:32,480 --> 00:46:33,720
I liked it.

472
00:46:33,720 --> 00:46:35,240
Can I kiss you again?

473
00:46:57,640 --> 00:46:59,680
That's enough.

474
00:46:59,680 --> 00:47:00,680
Enough already?

475
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:03,640
That's it?

476
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:36,680
Argh!

477
00:47:38,920 --> 00:47:41,200
Why hasn't Din replied yet?

478
00:47:41,200 --> 00:47:43,800
Did something happen?

479
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:44,800
Calm down.

480
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:46,880
Maybe he's talking to his mom.

481
00:47:46,880 --> 00:47:48,600
He'll reply soon.

482
00:47:48,600 --> 00:47:49,600
Don't overthink it.

483
00:47:49,600 --> 00:47:50,600
Easy.

484
00:47:50,600 --> 00:47:51,680
There, there.

485
00:47:53,440 --> 00:47:55,240
I want to believe that,

486
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:58,720
but what if Din really doesn't get in, Time?

487
00:47:59,880 --> 00:48:02,440
All we can do is comfort and support him, right?

488
00:48:02,760 --> 00:48:04,720
We can't do much more than that.

489
00:48:05,360 --> 00:48:07,080
Or do you think Din won't get in anywhere?

490
00:48:07,080 --> 00:48:08,680
No way.

491
00:48:09,320 --> 00:48:11,760
Exactly. I told you.

492
00:48:12,400 --> 00:48:14,840
Just wait for Din to reply. Don't overthink it.

493
00:48:34,240 --> 00:48:40,640
"Din, Star asked me to ask how your results turned out."

494
00:48:44,200 --> 00:48:47,640
Din, are your results out yet?

495
00:48:54,280 --> 00:48:58,000
If you want to decide for yourself, you have to deliver on what you said.

496
00:49:00,200 --> 00:49:01,200
Mom.

497
00:49:02,520 --> 00:49:03,840
I know you're worried,

498
00:49:04,760 --> 00:49:06,800
afraid I won't get in anywhere.

499
00:49:07,480 --> 00:49:09,120
But trust me.

500
00:49:11,080 --> 00:49:13,040
I'll get in through the quota round.

501
00:49:15,440 --> 00:49:18,600
Fine. But I have one more condition.

502
00:49:20,160 --> 00:49:21,680
If you don't get in this round,

503
00:49:21,680 --> 00:49:23,960
you'll go to the university I choose

504
00:49:23,960 --> 00:49:25,960
and the faculty I choose. Period.

505
00:49:30,760 --> 00:49:32,720
Do you understand me, Din?

506
00:49:54,640 --> 00:49:57,600
"Do you know he's been waiting for you? He took your words seriously."

507
00:49:57,600 --> 00:50:00,520
"But you left him. You vanished from his life. (Fuen)"

508
00:50:00,520 --> 00:50:02,200
"I'm going crazy. (Fuen)"

509
00:50:02,200 --> 00:50:06,800
"Sorry. We won't fight again, no matter what. (Physics)"

510
00:50:06,800 --> 00:50:09,600
"All I ask is one more chance."

511
00:50:09,600 --> 00:50:12,800
"I want you to get to know me before you decide. (Aof)"

512
00:50:12,800 --> 00:50:15,880
"If we're both still unsure of each other,"

513
00:50:15,880 --> 00:50:19,040
"why don't we try to make each other sure? (Star)"

514
00:50:19,040 --> 00:50:20,440
Confess.

515
00:50:20,440 --> 00:50:21,760
What about him?

516
00:50:22,480 --> 00:50:23,360
Does he like you?

517
00:50:24,400 --> 00:50:26,640
Guys, should we send the clip now?

518
00:50:26,640 --> 00:50:29,120
Send it. They say today's a lucky day,

519
00:50:29,120 --> 00:50:30,520
perfect for competing.

520
00:50:31,360 --> 00:50:31,960
Tired?

521
00:50:31,960 --> 00:50:34,600
Yeah, but I want to finish this page first.

522
00:50:35,240 --> 00:50:37,400
Smile. Be confident.

523
00:50:37,400 --> 00:50:38,840
Believe in yourself.

524
00:50:39,680 --> 00:50:43,880
Aof, I wrote a song. I'd like you to hear it.

525
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:47,960
Your mom doesn't know about Star at all?

526
00:50:47,960 --> 00:50:49,320
I never told her.

527
00:50:49,320 --> 00:50:50,760
It'll be okay, right, Din?

528
00:50:50,760 --> 00:50:51,760
That's so scary.

529
00:50:52,480 --> 00:50:54,200
I don't know.
